DP  - 2026 Jun 4
TI  - Content Validation of the AI-TPACK-E: Assessing AI Literacy Among Nurse 
      Educators.
LID - 10.1097/CIN.0000000000001576 [doi]
AB  - There is a critical need to assess nurse educators' competencies in artificial 
      intelligence (AI), yet no validated assessment tool currently exists to measure 
      their level of AI literacy. Developing such a tool is critical to guide targeted 
      educational strategies and inform curriculum design that prepares nursing 
      graduates for technology-enhanced health care. This paper presents the results of 
      content validity testing for an adapted 28-item Artificial Intelligence 
      Technology Pedagogical Content Knowledge and Ethics (AI-TPACK-E) scale, designed 
      to assess AI literacy among nurse educators from technological, pedagogical, 
      content, and ethical knowledge perspectives. Twelve content experts with relevant 
      experience in AI and nursing education evaluated the relevance of each item and 
      provided feedback for refinement. Item-level content validity (I-CVI) scores were 
      calculated, with ≥0.78 as the threshold for retaining items. The scale-level CVI 
      (S-CVI) using universal agreement (UA) was also computed. Results showed an 
      S-CVI/UA of 0.79, with 27 of 28 items achieving an I-CVI greater than 0.70 and 
      S-CVI-Average of 0.89. Experts emphasized the importance of the scale and 
      provided suggestions on item wording and the sequencing. These findings support 
      the preliminary content validity for the AI-TPACK-E scale for assessing nurse 
      educators' AI literacy. Planned future research includes pilot testing with a 
      larger sample of nurse educators to establish additional validity and reliability 
      evidence and examine their current AI integration practices in nursing education.
