TI  - AI Literacy as a Mediator Between Education Climate and Learning Agency in 
      Nursing Students.
LID - 10.1097/01.NEP.0000000000001547 [doi]
AB  - AIM: To examine the mediating role of artificial intelligence (AI) literacy in 
      the relationship between educational climate and student learning agency in 
      generative AI-supported contexts among nursing students. BACKGROUND: Fostering 
      learning agency is critical for preparing autonomous, engaged learners in the era 
      of AI. The influence of a supportive educational climate on learning agency may 
      depend on students' AI literacy. The interplay between them remains underexplored 
      in nursing education. METHOD: A cross-sectional survey was conducted from 
      February to March 2025 with 1,867 nursing students from seven junior colleges in 
      China. Students completed anonymous online questionnaires, including the 
      Educational Climate Inventory, AI Literacy Scale for Nonexperts, and the Student 
      Learning Agency in Generative AI-Supported Contexts (SLA-GAI) scale. RESULTS: 
      Educational climate and AI literacy were positively associated with SLA-GAI. AI 
      literacy partially mediated the relationship between educational climate and 
      student learning agency. CONCLUSION: Educational climate and AI literacy are key 
      to fostering SLA-GAI in nursing students. Integrating AI literacy training and 
      building supportive learning environments may better prepare students for 
      AI-integrated education and clinical practice.
