TI  - The association between generative artificial intelligence use and foreign 
      language classroom anxiety.
PG  - 107132
LID - S0001-6918(26)00933-9 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.actpsy.2026.107132 [doi]
AB  - This study examines the association between Generative Artificial Intelligence 
      use and foreign language classroom anxiety (FLCA) among undergraduates in an 
      under-resourced private university in Western China. Data were collected from 630 
      first- and second-year students using the Foreign Language Classroom Anxiety 
      Scale (FLCAS). Analyses included descriptive statistics, t-tests, analysis of 
      variance (ANOVA), Pearson correlations, and hierarchical regression. Results 
      showed that gender significantly predicted frequency of Artificial Intelligence 
      (AI) use (female > male, p < .01), but not FLCA or its two factors, Classroom 
      Performance Anxiety (CPA) and Learning Process Anxiety (LPA). English proficiency 
      significantly influenced both AI use frequency and FLCA (p < .05): 
      higher-proficiency students used AI more frequently but reported lower anxiety, 
      whereas age and socioeconomic status showed no significant effects. Regression 
      analyses indicated that, after controlling for proficiency, frequency of AI use 
      significantly predicted overall FLCA (B = 0.253, p < .001), CPA (B = 0.288, 
      p < .001), and LPA (B = 0.235, p < .001). Moderation analysis further showed that 
      English proficiency attenuated the relationship between AI use frequency and 
      anxiety, particularly for LPA. The final models explained 11.9% of the variance 
      in overall FLCA, 10.8% in CPA, and 11.3% in LPA. These findings suggest that 
      frequent AI use may be associated with heightened anxiety in under-resourced 
      contexts, while higher English proficiency serves an attenuating role, 
      underscoring the need for scaffolded AI literacy training and differentiated 
      instructional support when integrating AI tools.
