DP  - 2026 May 19
TI  - Reimagining Continuous Professional Development for Physicians in the Age of 
      Artificial Intelligence.
LID - 10.1097/CEH.0000000000000644 [doi]
AB  - Artificial intelligence (AI) is transforming medicine by changing how clinicians 
      learn, reason, communicate, and care for patients. Clinician expertise and 
      abilities extend beyond cognition and technical skill to include human capacities 
      like empathy, ethical discernment, moral responsibility, and trust-building with 
      patients. As AI becomes integral to health care, continuing professional 
      development (CPD) is increasingly positioned to support physicians in working 
      effectively with intelligent technology while preserving the human capacities 
      central to medical practice. CPD has long served clinicians by strengthening 
      foundational knowledge and reinforcing standards of care by delivering 
      high-quality, outcome-based education. Various educational models, designed for a 
      pre-AI era, emphasize knowledge acquisition over deeper clinical reasoning. Such 
      reasoning is now increasingly being augmented by AI-clinician collaboration in 
      contemporary practice. CPD can engage AI not only as a topic to study but as an 
      opportunity to reshape how physicians learn, reason, and approach clinical care. 
      This paper introduces the Technical Understanding, Critical Appraisal, and 
      Practical Application × Dual-Axis model, a framework supporting the coevolution 
      of individual and organizational learning for AI-enabled health care. This 
      conceptual framework integrates three domains of AI competency: Technical 
      Understanding, Critical Appraisal, and Practical Application with organizational 
      adoption and implementation strategies that focus on governance, infrastructure, 
      and culture. Linking personal AI literacy and fluency with institutional 
      capabilities creates a foundation for responsible AI in medicine. Reimagining CPD 
      with AI supports clinicians in developing adaptive expertise while remaining 
      clinically competent, ethically grounded, and compassionate while working 
      alongside AI models in a rapidly changing health care environment.
