MH  - *Patient Education as Topic/methods
MH  - Generative Artificial Intelligence
OAB - Many patients now ask artificial intelligence (AI) chatbots like ChatGPT and 
      Claude for health information about swallowing difficulties (dysphagia). We asked 
      both chatbots 46 common patient questions about dysphagia and had 10 medical 
      experts from five countries score the answers for accuracy, clarity, and 
      incorrect information. Both chatbots provided similarly accurate and clear 
      answers, scoring around 4 out of 5. However, the language used by both chatbots 
      was far too complex for most people to understand. The text required a college or 
      graduate‐level education to read, while health materials should be written at a 
      sixth‐grade level. This means that even when the information is correct, many 
      patients may not be able to understand it. AI chatbots show promise for providing 
      health information about dysphagia, but the language needs to be made much 
      simpler before patients can use them safely without a doctor's help.
