DP  - 2026
TI  - AI literacy among basic school teachers in Ghana: A structural equation modelling 
      analysis.
PG  - e0347117
LID - 10.1371/journal.pone.0347117 [doi]
LID - e0347117
AB  - Understanding the synergy of Artificial Intelligence (AI) literacy among teachers 
      is imperative for successful integration in educational settings. This study 
      examined basic school teachers' (BSTs) AI literacy based on four key aspects: AI 
      knowledge and understanding (KUAI), AI application (AAI), AI application 
      evaluation (EAIA), and AI ethics (AIE). The study employed a cross-sectional 
      survey design and purposive sampling to collect data from 319 BSTs in Ghana. A 
      variance-based structural equation modelling (VB-SEM) approach was used to 
      explore the relationships between these dimensions and provide insights into 
      their interrelationships. The study found that AAI positively influenced KUAI, 
      EAIA, and AIE. However, AIE did not significantly influence KUAI and EAAI. In 
      addition, KUAI did not influence EAIA. The findings contribute to understanding 
      the current state of AI literacy among BSTs in Ghana and highlight areas for 
      improvement in AI education and professional development programmes.
