TI  - From prompting to practice: Empowering faculty with AI and prompting tools.
PG  - 107096
LID - S0260-6917(26)00124-3 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.nedt.2026.107096 [doi]
AB  - As artificial intelligence (AI) transforms nursing education, faculty must 
      develop digital literacy and prompt engineering skills to integrate these tools 
      effectively. This paper explores how core nursing competencies align with prompt 
      engineering practices. Practical frameworks and examples support educators in 
      designing AI-assisted learning materials that strengthen engagement, 
      personalization, and competency-based instruction. By recognizing prompting as a 
      natural extension of familiar skills, nurse educators can confidently adopt AI to 
      enhance instructional design and student outcomes while maintaining pedagogical 
      integrity.
