TI  - Nurses confront artificial intelligence-generated health information at the 
      bedside: A case study.
PG  - 102738
LID - S0029-6554(26)00061-8 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.outlook.2026.102738 [doi]
AB  - As artificial intelligence (AI) tools increasingly shape how patients access 
      health information, nurses must navigate new bedside tensions. This case study 
      examines a nurse's encounter with a patient whose interpretation of AI‑generated 
      lab results conflicted with clinical evidence, fostering uncertainty. By 
      proposing theoretical frameworks grounded in bioethical principles, the case 
      explores how nurses can uphold the principles of autonomy, beneficence, and 
      justice when AI‑derived content influences patient decisions. Nurse‑led protocols 
      at the patient level (Ask, Balance, Clarify, Document) and team level (AI 
      Situation, Background, Assessment, Recommendation) are proposed to guide patient 
      education and communication when algorithmic outputs contradict standards of 
      care. The findings highlight the nurse's role as a mediator and underscore the 
      importance of AI literacy, transparency, and bias mitigation in nursing practice. 
      The study concludes with institutional implications, emphasizing the integration 
      of AI ethics into nursing education, governance structures, and 
      cross‑disciplinary collaboration.
