TI  - Experiences and Perspectives of Nursing Students and Educators on Artificial 
      Intelligence in Nursing Education: A Qualitative Systematic Review and 
      Meta-Synthesis.
LID - 10.1097/NNE.0000000000002147 [doi]
AB  - BACKGROUND: Artificial intelligence (AI) is transforming nursing education by 
      reshaping how knowledge is delivered, acquired, and applied. Synthesizing 
      qualitative evidence is essential for guiding ethical and human-centered AI 
      integration. PURPOSE: To interpret and synthesize qualitative evidence on nursing 
      students' and educators' experiences with AI-based educational interventions. 
      METHODS: Ten databases were searched. Methodological quality was appraised using 
      the Joanna Briggs Institute tool. Data were inductively coded and synthesized 
      through interpretive abstraction, and confidence in findings was evaluated using 
      ConQual. RESULTS: Thirty-four studies were included. A total of 141 themes and 
      169 subthemes were synthesized into 5 domains: facilitating deep learning and 
      clinical reasoning, fostering professional confidence and identity formation, 
      cultivating ethical awareness and critical reflection, integrating technology to 
      enhance pedagogical effectiveness, and navigating emotional and cognitive 
      challenges in AI-mediated learning. CONCLUSIONS: AI enhances engagement, 
      reasoning, confidence, and ethical reflection, yet concerns remain regarding 
      ethics, data security, and faculty preparedness.
