TI  - [Advantages and challenges of applying artificial intelligence in medical 
      education].
PG  - 200-206
LID - 10.3760/cma.j.cn112338-20250512-00309 [doi]
AB  - Although significant progress has been made in medical education in China, the 
      traditional education model is no longer capable of meeting the requirements for 
      cultivating high-quality medical talents in the current era. The rapid 
      development of artificial intelligence (AI) technology has created unprecedented 
      opportunities to transform traditional educational models. AI can optimize the 
      acquisition of medical information, provide students with timely and personalized 
      learning support, enhance clinical diagnosis and treatment capabilities, bridge 
      the gap between medical education and real-world practice, and improve teaching 
      efficiency and quality. However, the application of AI in medical education faces 
      several challenges. An intelligent medical education system that is efficient, 
      high-quality, and humanistic care is warranted. It is suggested to improve 
      top-level design and promote coordinated advancement in the intelligent 
      transformation of medical education; foster multi-party collaboration to develop 
      an "AI + medical education" agent; and enhance AI literacy among both teachers 
      and students, as well as form a new educational relationship of 
      "teacher-student-AI" trinity.
