JT  - Future oncology (London, England)
JID - 101256629
SB  - IM
MH  - Humans
MH  - *Neoplasms/psychology/therapy/diagnosis
MH  - Caregivers/psychology
PMC - PMC13051617
OAB - There are lots of places where people can look for information about cancer, for 
      example on websites or social media. People may also use AI (artificial 
      intelligence) tools as a starting point to help pull information together. Some 
      information can be useful, but some can be hard to make sense of, or even untrue, 
      and some may only relate to particular types of cancer, which could lead to 
      unrealistic expectations of treatment options and outcomes. How can people with 
      cancer and their families be sure that they are finding the best information for 
      their needs? This podcast talks through the challenges and offers ideas to help 
      people find and understand trustworthy health information. It comes with a 
      patient’s guide to cancer-focused medical journals, which explains what journals 
      are and the types of patient-friendly content that they can contain. As well as 
      being for people with cancer and their families, the podcast is also for doctors 
      and other healthcare providers who want to help their patients. Healthcare 
      providers have an important role in helping their patients find good quality 
      information about their own particular type of cancer. We encourage patients to 
      ask their healthcare providers questions about where to find information and what 
      it means.
