OAB - Endocrine hypertension happens when hormone-producing glands – like the adrenal 
      or thyroid – cause high blood pressure. Detecting these cases early can often 
      lead to a cure, but diagnosis is complex. Researchers are now using powerful 
      computer tools (artificial intelligence) and ‘omics’ technologies that study 
      genes, proteins, and body chemicals together. These approaches help doctors find 
      the specific cause of hypertension faster and more accurately. This review 
      explains how combining AI with advanced laboratory testing may soon replace some 
      invasive procedures. Although more studies and better access to technology are 
      still needed, these innovations could make diagnosis easier, treatments more 
      personalized, and outcomes better for people with hormonal causes of high blood 
      pressure.
