TI  - Artificial Intelligence in Pediatric Practice: Controversies, Policy, and 
      Practical Pointers forNurse Practitioners.
PG  - 308-317
LID - S0891-5245(25)00419-5 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.pedhc.2025.12.014 [doi]
AB  - Artificial intelligence (AI) is rapidly transforming pediatric healthcare, yet 
      many pediatric nurse practitioners lack adequate preparation for implementation. 
      This article provides foundational AI literacy while examining urgent needs for 
      comprehensive policy frameworks, collaborative governance, and meaningful patient 
      engagement in training data decisions. AI literacy must precede widespread 
      implementation: practitioners, policymakers, and patients must understand how 
      generative AI models work, how training data shapes outcomes, and ramifications 
      of algorithmic bias. Drawing on recent literature, this discussion addresses 
      practical clinical considerations and the critical advocacy role PNPs must play 
      in shaping equitable, transparent, and accountable AI systems in healthcare.
