TI  - The Mediating Effect of Professional Commitment Between Environmental Support on 
      Campus and AI Literacy Among Nursing Students: A Cross-Sectional Study.
PG  - E206-E212
LID - 10.1097/NNE.0000000000002103 [doi]
AB  - BACKGROUND: With AI technologies increasingly integrated into nursing education, 
      enhancing AI literacy among nursing students is critical, yet influencing factors 
      remain understudied. PURPOSE: This study assessed AI literacy levels among 
      nursing students, identified key influencing factors, and examined the mediating 
      role of professional commitment between campus environmental support and AI 
      literacy. METHODS: A cross-sectional survey was conducted with 1680 nursing 
      students from 6 medical colleges in Anhui Province, China, using convenience 
      sampling. Data were collected through structured scales and analyzed via multiple 
      linear regression and mediation models. RESULTS: AI literacy was moderately high, 
      positively influenced by urban residence and prior AI training. Campus support 
      directly enhanced it (β = 0.675), with professional commitment serving as a 
      partial mediator (indirect β = 1.857). CONCLUSIONS: To enhance AI literacy, 
      increasing campus AI resources, improving educational environments, and 
      strengthening professional commitment are recommended, integrating AI competency 
      into nursing education.
