TI  - Generative AI in consumer health: leveraging large language models for health 
      literacy and clinical safety with a digital health framework.
PG  - 1616488
LID - 10.3389/fdgth.2025.1616488 [doi]
LID - 1616488
AB  - Generative AI, powered by large language models, is transforming consumer health 
      by enhancing health literacy and delivering personalized health education. 
      However, ensuring clinical safety and effectiveness requires a robust digital 
      health framework to address risks like misinformation and inequitable 
      communication. This mini review examines current use cases for generative AI in 
      consumer health education, highlights persistent challenges, and proposes a 
      clinician-informed framework to evaluate safety, usability, and effectiveness. 
      The RECAP model-Relevance, Evidence-based, Clarity, Adaptability, and 
      Precision-offers a pragmatic lens to guide responsible implementation of AI in 
      patient-facing tools. By connecting insights from past digital health innovations 
      to the opportunities and pitfalls of large language models, this paper provides 
      both context and direction for future development.
