AB  - This manuscript presents key advances of the Antibacterial Resistance Leadership 
      Group (ARLG) Innovations Task Force, a collaboration focused on improving 
      endpoints for registrational trials of antibacterial drugs, including 
      health-related quality-of-life measures, for common acute infections. This group 
      includes members from the United States Food and Drug Administration, National 
      Institutes of Health, academia, industry, and patient representatives to amplify 
      patient voices and ensure that the endpoints are meaningful to how patients feel, 
      function, and survive.
