TI  - Engagement Strategies for Digital Literacy to Support the Brazilian e-SUS Primary 
      Care System.
PG  - 1422-1426
LID - 10.3233/SHTI251073 [doi]
AB  - Massive Open Online Courses (MOOCs) offer scalable solutions for professional 
      training but face challenges such as high dropout rates and low completion rates. 
      This study explores engagement strategies in the Educa e-SUS APS platform, a MOOC 
      designed for Brazilian Primary Health Care professionals. Key interventions 
      included gamification, audiovisual resources, and personalized re-engagement 
      messages supported by a Large Language Model (LLM). LLM-driven strategies 
      addressed dropouts by crafting tailored messages, achieving a re-engagement rate 
      exceeding 12%. Results showed improved completion rates compared to global MOOC 
      averages, underscoring the effectiveness of integrating modern pedagogical 
      approaches and personalized communication. These findings highlight the potential 
      of MOOCs, supported by AI, to enhance learner retention and advance digital 
      education in public health systems.
