TI  - The Emerging Role of Generative Artificial Intelligence in Medical Education, 
      Research, and Practice.
PG  - e40883
LID - 10.7759/cureus.40883 [doi]
LID - e40883
AB  - Recent breakthroughs in generative artificial intelligence (GAI) and the 
      emergence of transformer-based large language models such as Chat Generative 
      Pre-trained Transformer (ChatGPT) have the potential to transform healthcare 
      education, research, and clinical practice. This article examines the current 
      trends in using GAI models in medicine, outlining their strengths and 
      limitations. It is imperative to develop further consensus-based guidelines to 
      govern the appropriate use of GAI, not only in medical education but also in 
      research, scholarship, and clinical practice.
