TI  - Identification and characterization of learning weakness from drawing analysis at 
      the pre-literacy stage.
PG  - 21624
LID - 10.1038/s41598-022-26038-9 [doi]
LID - 21624
AB  - Handwriting learning delays should be addressed early to prevent their 
      exacerbation and long-lasting consequences on whole children's lives. Ideally, 
      proper training should start even before learning how to write. This work 
      presents a novel method to disclose potential handwriting problems, from a 
      pre-literacy stage, based on drawings instead of words production analysis. Two 
      hundred forty-one kindergartners drew on a tablet, and we computed features known 
      to be distinctive of poor handwriting from symbols drawings. We verified that 
      abnormal features patterns reflected abnormal drawings, and found correspondence 
      in experts' evaluation of the potential risk of developing a learning delay in 
      the graphical sphere. A machine learning model was able to discriminate with 0.75 
      sensitivity and 0.76 specificity children at risk. Finally, we explained why 
      children were considered at risk by the algorithms to inform teachers on the 
      specific weaknesses that need training. Thanks to this system, early intervention 
      to train specific learning delays will be finally possible.
