TI  - Standardized Reporting of Machine Learning Applications in Urology: The 
      STREAM-URO Framework.
PG  - 672-682
LID - S2405-4569(21)00183-8 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.euf.2021.07.004 [doi]
AB  - The Standardized Reporting of Machine Learning Applications in Urology 
      (STREAM-URO) framework was developed to provide a set of recommendations to help 
      standardize how machine learning studies in urology are reported. This framework 
      serves three purposes: (1) to promote high-quality studies and streamline the 
      peer review process; (2) to enhance reproducibility, comparability, and 
      interpretability of results; and (3) to improve engagement and literacy of 
      machine learning within the urological community.
