TI  - [For discussion: What potential does digitization hold for patient safety?].
PG  - 52-59
LID - S1865-9217(19)30098-4 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.zefq.2019.07.005 [doi]
AB  - Digitization is comparatively underdeveloped in the German healthcare system. 
      Many digital applications are potentially capable of improving patient safety. 
      This potential cannot be exploited in the long term with regional and 
      time-limited projects. The present article identifies care areas where digital 
      solutions are possible and necessary for safe patient care. In order for digital 
      solutions and applications to be available to policyholders in the first 
      healthcare market, producer of eHealth solutions will have to consider the goals 
      of patient safety from the very beginning. In addition, processes and structures 
      for proof of benefit must be implemented. (As supplied by publisher).
