TI  - Machine Learning to Identify Behavioral Determinants of Oral Health in Inner City 
      Older Hispanic Adults.
PG  - 253-256
AB  - We applied machine learning techniques to a community-based behavioral dataset to 
      build prediction models to gain insights about minority dental health and 
      population aging as the foundation for future interventions for urban Hispanics. 
      Our application of machine learning techniques identified emotional and systemic 
      factors such as chronic stress and health literacy as the strongest predictors of 
      self-reported dental health among hundreds of possible variables. Application of 
      machine learning algorithms was useful to build prediction models to gain 
      insights about dental health and minority population aging.
