TI  - Candidate hepatitis C vaccine trials and people who inject drugs: challenges and 
      opportunities.
PG  - 7273-8
LID - 10.1016/j.vaccine.2010.08.085 [doi]
AB  - People who inject drugs (PWID) are at high risk of HCV. Limited evidence of the 
      effectiveness of prevention interventions and low uptake of treatment in this 
      group highlight the need for increased investment in biomedical interventions, 
      notably safe and efficacious vaccines. While several candidates are currently in 
      development, field trials in PWID present challenges, including ethical issues 
      associated with trial literacy, informed consent and standards of care. 
      Significant biological and social factors and differences between HIV and HCV 
      suggest that HCV warrants targeted vaccine preparedness research to lay the 
      groundwork for successful implementation of future trials.
