TI  - AutoTutor: a tutor with dialogue in natural language.
PG  - 180-92
AB  - AutoTutor is a learning environment that tutors students by holding a 
      conversation in natural language. AutoTutor has been developed for Newtonian 
      qualitative physics and computer literacy. Its design was inspired by 
      explanation-based constructivist theories of learning, intelligent tutoring 
      systems that adaptively respond to student knowledge, and empirical research on 
      dialogue patterns in tutorial discourse. AutoTutor presents challenging problems 
      (formulated as questions) from a curriculum script and then engages in mixed 
      initiative dialogue that guides the student in building an answer. It provides 
      the student with positive, neutral, or negative feedback on the student's typed 
      responses, pumps the student for more information, prompts the student to fill in 
      missing words, gives hints, fills in missing information with assertions, 
      identifies and corrects erroneous ideas, answers the student's questions, and 
      summarizes answers. AutoTutor has produced learning gains of approximately .70 
      sigma for deep levels of comprehension.
